00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A SPECIAL MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, JANUARY 16, 2008\r\rMayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 6:35 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 6:36 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Personnel Matter, pursuant to Government Code, Section 54957:\r PUBLIC EMPLOYEE PERFORMANCE EVALUATION, Title: City Manager.\r\rReal property negotiations, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.8.\rAgency Negotiator:�� Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director.\rNegotiating parties:�� City of Calabasas and Currey-Riach / RCS Development.\rInstruction: Discussion regarding negotiations on lot located on southwest corner of Lost Hills and Calabasas Hills Roads.\rIdentity of property:��Assessors Parcel Number 2063-043-015.�\r\rPending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a): Calabasas Ridge HOA v. Gordon, LC 079145; Smith v. City of Calabasas, BS 106644; Cooper v. Calabasas Park Estates Owners Association,�BC 323695; Toby Keeler & Elizabeth Stephens v. City of Calabasas, BS 109503; Parks v. City of Calabasas, BC 382012.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:30 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Annemarie Flaherty.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, reported that, in closed session, the City Council authorized the City Attorney to defend the City as joint counsel in a lawsuit entitled Parks v. City of Calabasas, and stated that the Council presented a favorable performance evaluation to the City Manager.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor Bozajian introduced Annemarie Flaherty, the new Executive Director of the Agoura Hills/Calabasas Community Center. Mayor Bozajian introduced Rudy Gonzales of Southern California Edison who presented the �State of the Utility System�. Mayor Bozajian introduced the presidents of the Parent Faculty Clubs for schools in Calabasas and the City Council presented them with grant checks from the City�s Education Fund. Mayor pro Tem Maurer spoke regarding the upcoming Chamber of Commerce Installation Dinner. Mayor Bozajian spoke regarding the upcoming State of the City address on February 13, 2008 and the opening of the Las Virgenes Creek Restoration project. Mayor Bozajian also spoke regarding the upcoming Primary Election and encouraged everyone to vote.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Anthony Pecoraro, Calabasas, spoke regarding affordable housing issues in the City of Calabasas.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the January 2, 2008 City Council meeting.\r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2008-242, amending Chapter 3.40 of the Calabasas Municipal Code relating to the Purchasing System.\r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2008-239, restricting smoking in multi-family rental housing.\r\r Recommendation to award a professional services agreement for City Prosecutor services to Dapeer, Rosenblit & Litvak, LLP, in the amount of $250,000.\r\r Recommendation to approve Amendment #2 to the professional services agreement for as-needed specialty inspection and testing services in the amount of $75,000 to Twinings Laboratories of Southern California.\r\r Recommendation to rescind the contract originally awarded to VanderGeest Landscape Care for Specification No. 07-08-06, landscape maintenance of public works street medians and certain sidewalk and parkway areas within the City of Calabasas; and to award the contract to the next lowest responsive bidder,Valleycrest Landscape Maintenance.\r\r Recommendation to rescind the contract originally awarded to VanderGeest Landscape Care for Specification No. 07-08-07, landscape maintenance of City parks within the City of Calabasas; and to award the contract to the next lowest responsive bidder, Venco Western Landscape, Inc. \r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, and 5. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rSteven Rosenblit, new City Prosecutor, introduced himself to the City Council.\r\rTara Bannister, California Apartment Association, supports the City�s proposed ordinance to restrict smoking in rental housing.\r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve Consent Items #3, 4, 6 and 7. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rPUBLIC HEARINGS\r\r Recommendation to continue the public hearing for the introduction of Ordinance 2008-243, prohibiting the operation of mobile car wash businesses in the City of Calabasas.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson to table the item. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Review and approval of projects for the 34th Program Year (2008-2009) � Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) Funding; and adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1112, approving the CDBG 34th Program Year (2008-2009).\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rTina Gall, Community Development Block Grant Consultant, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\rMayor pro Tem Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve the projects for the 34th Program Year and adopt Resolution No. 2008-1112. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1111, repealing Resolution No. 2004-906 and establishing diversion goals, rates, fees, surcharges, and permit renewal parameters for the collection, transportation and disposal of municipal solid waste,� and recyclable material within the City of Calabasas.\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rAlex Farassati, Environmental Services Manager, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to adopt Resolution No. 2008-1111, establishing diversion goals, rates, fees, surcharges, and permit renewal parameters for the collection, transportation and disposal of municipal solid waste,� and recyclable material within the City of Calabasas. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1110, approving a street name change from Park Centre to Civic Center Way.\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to adopt Resolution No. 2008-1110, approving a street name change from Park Centre to Civic Center Way. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1115, approving the removal of one heritage oak tree and one non-heritage oak tree and encroachment into the protected zone of three non-heritage oak trees in order to construct a seventy-five unit affordable senior housing development for households earning between thirty and sixty percent of the Area Median Income, with a subterranean parking garage at 4803 El Canon Avenue, in the Commercial, Old Town (CT) zoning district.\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rTalyn Mirzakhanian, Planner, presented the staff report.\r\rFred Gaines, on behalf of Thomas Safran & Associates, spoke in support of the proposed recommendation.\r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to adopt Resolution No. 2008-1115, approving the removal of one heritage oak tree and one non-heritage oak tree and encroachment into the protected zone of three non-heritage oak trees. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r\r\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Consideration of a request by Thomas Safran Associates Inc. for $750,000 from the affordable housing trust fund for a seventy-five unit affordable senior housing development for households earning between thirty and sixty percent of the Area Median Income at 4803 El Canon Ave.\r\rTalyn Mirzakhanian, Planner, presented the staff report.\r\rAnthony Pecoraro, Calabasas, spoke in support of the proposed project and spoke in support of loaning the applicant $1,000,000 rather than the requested $750,000. Andrew Gross and Tom Safran, representing Thomas Safran & Associates, provided background information on the request for funds.\r\r Mayor pro Tem Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve a loan commitment of $1,000,000 from the affordable housing trust fund with the following conditions:\rThat the developer has 2 years to demonstrate that he has full funding for the project;\rThat an interest list for the project be generated. \rMOTION CARRIED 4/1. Mayor Bozajian voted NO.\r\rThe following item was heard out of order of the agenda:\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r Discussion of lobbyist action plan for 101 Freeway Interchange at Lost Hills Road to secure federal funding for construction of the bridge.\r\rThe City Council provided direction to staff to schedule a delegation to travel to Washington.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of December 20, 2007 to January 3, 2008.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Councilmember Wolfson provided an update on the Civic Center project.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r The City Manager indicated he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r \r The City Council requested the following items be agendized for discussion:\r\rHistoric Preservation Commission appointments;\rA report from Councilmember Washburn on items discussed at an upcoming conference in Yosemite;\rDiscussion regarding �bundling� of technology services.\r\rADJOURN \r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:58 p.m. in memory of Linda Bloom and Marilyn Ginsberg.\r\r\r_____________________________\rRobin Parker, City Clerk\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 6 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r01/16/08\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00